Subject: Preserve original allocator with native pointer and block alignment

Upstream-base: 45f25bd6519586837e61251208d34d8dcf94e170

Keep the original start/end allocation, circular free-list, relative 32-bit trailer,
coalescing, and free-memory statistics algorithms. Native addresses use uintptr_t;
split blocks align to the native free-list type and its actual size replaces 12-byte
assumptions. Native invalid arenas/alignment and allocation exhaustion throw errors
instead of using target panic/file-dump paths or looping forever. This does not
establish exact console allocation layout, full diagnostics, or thread safety.

